---
import StudioLayout from '../../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import { studioCalendarNotes } from '../../../lib/studioHelp';
---

<StudioLayout
  title="Calendar help"
  description="Private guide to Studio lesson scheduling and Google Calendar."
  heading="Calendar help"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-4 py-5 md:py-8">
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a href="/studio/help" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        ← All help
      </a>
      {' · '}
      <a href="/studio/calendar" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        Open Schedules
      </a>
    </p>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">{studioCalendarNotes.title}</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">{studioCalendarNotes.summary}</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>
          Connect Google under{' '}
          <a href="/studio/admin/calendar" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Admin → Calendar</a>
          {' '}(Connect Google permission). The Studio organizer account creates the invite. Elyse’s
          own Google is optional and only used to read busy time.
        </li>
        <li>
          Request a time under{' '}
          <a href="/studio/calendar" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Students → Schedules</a>.
          The student sees <span class="text-spotlight">Requested</span> until Elyse accepts.
        </li>
        <li>
          Elyse <span class="text-spotlight">Accepts</span> the invite in Google Calendar on her
          phone. Studio then marks the lesson <span class="text-spotlight">Confirmed</span>.
        </li>
        <li>
          If Google is disconnected, the request is still saved. Elyse gets an email with a
          calendar file (ICS) and Confirm / Decline links.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">Requested vs Confirmed</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        <span class="text-spotlight">Requested</span> means the time is held in Studio and Elyse
        has an invite. <span class="text-spotlight">Confirmed</span> means she accepted (Google) or
        tapped Confirm in Studio / the email link when Google is down. Decline or cancel one week
        does not delete a weekly series.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">Weekly series</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        A weekly student can be booked for up to <span class="text-spotlight">12 weeks</span> (one
        quarter). Canceling one week leaves the rest of the series.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-spotlight">Google is the calendar</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Studio does not keep a second calendar of times. Busy time comes from the Google calendars
        Elyse selects. The public site, People, payments, and publish keep working when Google is
        down.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</StudioLayout>
